WEBVTT

1
00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:26.800
I'm not the...

2
00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:29.320
smartest person
on this planet.

3
00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:31.880
I'm not the most skilled person
on this planet.

4
00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:33.360
I, um...

5
00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:36.240
I'm not the best looking
or whatever.

6
00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:38.320
I don't have
the best background.

7
00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:40.200
All these kind of things.
But it's not a problem at all.

8
00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:47.880
My two best friends had the best
grades from the whole school

9
00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:50.960
and we were learning together
and I was not even close to them

10
00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:52.800
and I didn't think,
"I'm a bit...

11
00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:54.360
dumb" or whatever.

12
00:00:56.680 --> 00:00:59.640
I just took it like it is
and knew that's my basis

13
00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:00.800
from here,
I have to jump.

14
00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:05.600
What I want to say with it is

15
00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:09.240
I always felt support
from people

16
00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:11.880
from my friends, from my family
all the way through.

17
00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:15.920
When you walk through a storm

18
00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:17.960
and there are different storms
out there

19
00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:20.520
that's the moment
when you need support.

20
00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:23.840
and I really love the fact

21
00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:28.120
that there is a song
about my way of life.

22
00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:29.680
How I understand life.

23
00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:34.120
You'll never walk alone.

24
00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:36.360
It was not the reason
why I came here.

25
00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:37.840
It's a pure coincidence.

26
00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:45.720
It's my anthem for years
and years.

27
00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:48.800
I think it's in one of the most
beautiful songs ever.

28
00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:53.880
That's it. So here we are.
and it's a pretty good fit.

29
00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:58.440
[CROWD CHEERS
AND WHISTLES]

30
00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:01.800
[BOY]: Liverpool Football Club,
it means life. Honestly.

31
00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:03.360
[MUSIC: "Liverpool"
sung by Chelcee Grimes]

32
00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:05.200
♪ We got some history
don't we? ♪

33
00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:08.640
♪ No one knows me
like you know me ♪

34
00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:12.720
♪ Hardest thing
I ever did was go ♪

35
00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:15.160
My grandfather followed
Liverpool all over Europe.

36
00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:16.520
It's just ingrained in us.

37
00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:18.880
♪ We both knew
that this would happen ♪

38
00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:22.520
♪ And you stole my heart
in the cavern ♪

39
00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:25.960
♪ We shared things
that nobody knows ♪

40
00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:27.280
[DALGLISH]:
People used to say

41
00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:29.400
"What was the secret
Liverpool Football Club?"

42
00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:31.840
If they had a secret,
we wouldn't tell you.

43
00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:34.880
[CROWD CHEERS]

44
00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:37.800
The supporters
have always had huge effect.

45
00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:41.520
[AHMED CAIRO IN ARABIC]:

46
00:02:45.320 --> 00:02:47.440
[NEWS READER]: The death toll
from the stadium disaster

47
00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:49.440
stands at 96.

48
00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:51.560
[WOMAN]:
When Liverpool play

49
00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:54.560
it's a combination of excitement
and fear.

50
00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:55.680
You never know
what's gonna happen.

51
00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:59.120
[COMMENTATOR]:
Joy for Manchester United!

52
00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:00.760
I was six when
we last won the league

53
00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:02.160
and to be honest,
I don't remember it.

54
00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:06.440
[CROWD CHEERS]

55
00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:10.040
[COMMENTATOR]:
Ryan Giggs has scored!

56
00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:12.000
[THIERRY HENRY]:
It seems to me like

57
00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:13.760
they don't really like football.

58
00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:16.120
It's not a big team anymore.

59
00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:21.720
[IN MANDARIN]:

60
00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:28.360
[COMMENTATOR]: Gerrard,
with the shot. Oh, what a goal!

61
00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:32.720
[COMMENTATOR]:
Oh, Gerrard slipped.

62
00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:34.200
And Demba Ba's in here!

63
00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:37.720
Ba punishes, of all people...
Steven Gerrard.

64
00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:40.000
[WOMAN]: I just cried
and cried and cried

65
00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:42.240
and I just felt like
my entire world

66
00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:43.280
had come crashing down.

67
00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:47.280
[MAN IN ARABIC]:

68
00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:52.920
[PRESENTER]: Big breaking
news for the Premier League.

69
00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:55.360
Brendan Rodgers
has left Liverpool.

70
00:03:55.880 --> 00:03:57.120
Where do they go next then?

71
00:03:57.280 --> 00:03:58.280
I would go for Klopp.

72
00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:02.120
Liverpool appears to be
closing in on a new manager.

73
00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:03.880
The German Jurgen Klopp.

74
00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:07.000
The day that Jurgen
was appointed I said

75
00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:10.000
"Fasten your seat belts.
We're off and running here".

76
00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:11.920
He's a breath of fresh air.

77
00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:13.680
He said that he's going to
win us the Premiership.

78
00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:14.680
It's what we want.

79
00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:19.080
In this moment, we are not
the best team in the world.

80
00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:22.040
They don't believe in
this moment, yeah?

81
00:04:22.120 --> 00:04:24.680
So they only want to see,
OK, five years ago

82
00:04:24.760 --> 00:04:25.960
ten years ago,
20 years ago.

83
00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:30.400
History is great,
but it's only to remember.

84
00:04:31.320 --> 00:04:35.240
Now we have the possibility
to write a new story.

85
00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:38.920
♪ I hope you know it's true ♪

86
00:04:39.480 --> 00:04:42.560
♪ Oh, I miss you Liverpool ♪

87
00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:52.880
[CROWD CHEERS]

88
00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:55.520
[REPORTER]: Jurgen Klopp
arriving here at the Lane.

89
00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:57.880
He's a manager who's worked
wonders in the Bundesliga.

90
00:04:57.960 --> 00:05:00.280
Twice managing Dortmund to
the League Championship there.

91
00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:03.760
Can he bring similar successes
to Merseyside?

92
00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:09.840
Usually in life
you have to fulfil

93
00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:11.600
first and foremost
your own expectations.

94
00:05:14.320 --> 00:05:17.400
But when you come to Liverpool,
then it's completely different

95
00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:22.240
because there's so many people
dream about our success.

96
00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:30.920
Winning trophies is fulfilling
the expectations of the people.

97
00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:36.560
My first game at Tottenham

98
00:05:38.080 --> 00:05:40.080
I always watched the other team
warming up.

99
00:05:40.720 --> 00:05:42.960
Tottenham, they're good looking.
Dark blue.

100
00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:45.120
Harry Kane, Dele Alli.

101
00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:46.440
Everything looks set.

102
00:05:46.960 --> 00:05:48.640
You turn around. Wow!

103
00:05:49.760 --> 00:05:51.400
We all look like Captain Picard.

104
00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:55.440
The wrong sizes, they didn't fit
really the players.

105
00:05:57.520 --> 00:05:58.960
I was not happy.

106
00:05:59.440 --> 00:06:00.600
And I thought:
how can you be...

107
00:06:00.680 --> 00:06:04.400
the game didn't even start,
being already the second best.

108
00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:08.520
[CROWD CHEERS]
- [COMMENTATOR]: It's Harry Kane

109
00:06:08.600 --> 00:06:10.320
and this is N'Jie
with the finish!

110
00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:14.480
[KLOPP]: So next day,
I asked for a meeting

111
00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:15.480
and said, "Hey, come on.

112
00:06:15.800 --> 00:06:17.280
What can we change immediately?"

113
00:06:17.800 --> 00:06:18.680
Because I really think that

114
00:06:18.760 --> 00:06:20.400
these kind of things
are important.

115
00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:23.120
[COMMENTATOR]:
He's gonna break for Harry Kane!

116
00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:26.400
[KLOPP]:
I'm not a control freak.

117
00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:29.680
I just think things should
happen in a specific way.

118
00:06:42.320 --> 00:06:44.080
[COMMENTATOR]:
Forward looking for Ighalo.

119
00:06:44.280 --> 00:06:46.600
Who is really quick
and persistent.

120
00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:48.880
And he reaps the reward!

121
00:06:51.120 --> 00:06:52.640
Well, Lallana with the header.

122
00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:55.680
You do sense that Liverpool will
eventually create something.

123
00:06:55.760 --> 00:06:57.520
They've still not had
a shot on target.

124
00:06:58.400 --> 00:06:59.640
[KLOPP]:
We have some problems.

125
00:06:59.720 --> 00:07:01.800
You have to solve them.
So I need help.

126
00:07:01.880 --> 00:07:04.840
Of course,
we have to find good defenders

127
00:07:04.920 --> 00:07:06.640
good strikers, good midfielders.

128
00:07:07.680 --> 00:07:08.920
[REPORTER]:
The breaking news is that

129
00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:12.160
Liverpool have completed
the signing of Sadio Mane

130
00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:13.240
from Southampton.

131
00:07:13.720 --> 00:07:14.880
[COMMENTATOR]:
Sigurdsson...

132
00:07:15.440 --> 00:07:18.280
looking deep for Fernandez,
who wins it

133
00:07:18.520 --> 00:07:19.640
and it's still not away

134
00:07:19.840 --> 00:07:22.200
and it's in by
Fernando Llorente.

135
00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:25.200
It's a lovely ball as well.
It's two!

136
00:07:25.600 --> 00:07:27.560
That was poorly defended
by Liverpool.

137
00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:29.360
We need a leader,
at the back.

138
00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:31.360
[REPORTER]:
Big transfer story tonight.

139
00:07:31.440 --> 00:07:34.960
Liverpool have got their man,
Virgil van Dijk.

140
00:07:35.560 --> 00:07:38.120
[KLOPP]: I'm not a genius,
so I cannot do it alone.

141
00:07:40.520 --> 00:07:42.160
[COMMENTATOR]:
Oh, Karius has lost it!

142
00:07:42.240 --> 00:07:44.040
And it's in by Nathan Ake!

143
00:07:44.120 --> 00:07:47.640
It is just a horrible,
horrible day for Liverpool.

144
00:07:47.760 --> 00:07:50.560
[REPORTER]: Liverpool have
confirmed the world record

145
00:07:50.640 --> 00:07:54.640
for a goalkeeper signing
of Alisson from Roma.

146
00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:58.760
[IN PORTUGUESE]:

147
00:08:05.760 --> 00:08:06.760
[HE LAUGHS]

148
00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:08.200
[HE YELLS]

149
00:08:32.280 --> 00:08:33.320
Morning.

150
00:08:53.440 --> 00:08:58.360
[PLAYERS SHOUT]

151
00:08:58.480 --> 00:09:00.920
[HENDERSON]: As captain of
a football club like Liverpool

152
00:09:01.360 --> 00:09:03.520
what your role is,
what you're here to do

153
00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:06.240
is get the best out of yourself
get the best out of the team.

154
00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:08.760
Setting the standard

155
00:09:08.840 --> 00:09:11.080
making sure you've given
everything every single day.

156
00:09:11.240 --> 00:09:13.160
And eventually
you'll get your rewards.

157
00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:17.360
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

158
00:09:17.560 --> 00:09:19.120
But, it doesn't stop here.

159
00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:21.200
You know, you gotta keep going.
You gotta keep improving.

160
00:09:23.840 --> 00:09:25.400
[VAN DIJK]: It's never easy
in pre-season.

161
00:09:26.560 --> 00:09:27.920
You start from scratch.

162
00:09:29.320 --> 00:09:34.280
What happened three weeks ago,
four weeks ago, is gone.

163
00:09:37.920 --> 00:09:41.520
Winning the Champions League was
a dream come true for myself.

164
00:09:42.320 --> 00:09:44.760
The celebration we had
with the fans, the parade.

165
00:09:44.840 --> 00:09:45.880
[FIREWORK BANGS]

166
00:09:47.600 --> 00:09:50.520
Definitely,
I want to experience this again.

167
00:09:54.800 --> 00:09:56.320
[REPORTER]:
Champions of Europe.

168
00:09:56.400 --> 00:09:57.200
But it's all about being

169
00:09:57.280 --> 00:09:59.480
Champions of England now
surely.

170
00:09:59.640 --> 00:10:01.720
[KLOPP]: Last year we had
the determination

171
00:10:01.800 --> 00:10:04.440
we had the desire, the emotion,
the passion.

172
00:10:05.280 --> 00:10:07.000
The boys played
an exceptional season.

173
00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:10.240
But we have to make
the next step.

174
00:10:11.240 --> 00:10:13.000
[COMMENTATOR]:
Coming out on top again

175
00:10:13.080 --> 00:10:15.760
in the Premier League,
Manchester City!

176
00:10:16.080 --> 00:10:17.040
[VAN DIJK]:
Last year...

177
00:10:17.160 --> 00:10:20.600
the Premier League, City was
just a little bit better.

178
00:10:31.240 --> 00:10:35.920
A lot of it is mentally how we
deal with things under pressure.

179
00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:48.800
What up and good morning!
We're back in Nazare.

180
00:10:49.520 --> 00:10:52.360
I remember I saw
a little video on social media.

181
00:10:54.400 --> 00:10:58.480
Someone on a wave and the wave
was miles in the air.

182
00:11:00.200 --> 00:11:01.400
[STEUDTNER] We're going to take
you guys with us

183
00:11:01.520 --> 00:11:04.080
to show you a little bit
about Nazare

184
00:11:04.360 --> 00:11:06.520
and the preparations
before the season starts.

185
00:11:07.160 --> 00:11:08.760
[KLOPP]: Sebastian Steudtner
is a German guy.

186
00:11:08.840 --> 00:11:11.240
He's the world's best
high wave surfer.

187
00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:12.360
Wow.

188
00:11:12.440 --> 00:11:15.400
He's all the time
in a life-threatening situation.

189
00:11:15.800 --> 00:11:18.440
And if he surfs the highest
wave he ever saw

190
00:11:18.520 --> 00:11:20.400
then he's looking for the next
highest wave

191
00:11:20.480 --> 00:11:22.080
and he's waiting for that
the whole year.

192
00:11:22.160 --> 00:11:23.320
Maybe two years,
maybe three years.

193
00:11:24.280 --> 00:11:28.640
It's just so obvious where
the similarities are.

194
00:11:30.560 --> 00:11:31.960
[VAN DIJK]:
So we met him.

195
00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:34.880
I was very, very interested
in what he had to say

196
00:11:35.240 --> 00:11:37.600
about how he deals
with pressure.

197
00:11:38.960 --> 00:11:42.880
He's like you need
to do one little slight mistake

198
00:11:42.960 --> 00:11:44.280
and life could be over.

199
00:11:47.920 --> 00:11:49.280
Shall we swim?

200
00:11:51.840 --> 00:11:53.360
[VAN DIJK]: After that,
we went to the pool

201
00:11:53.440 --> 00:11:55.480
and did a little bit of
breathing techniques.

202
00:11:55.720 --> 00:11:58.400
[INDISTINCT CHATTER
AND LAUGHTER]

203
00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:02.000
You had to stay underwater
for as long as you can

204
00:12:02.080 --> 00:12:04.840
and I remember I was there
for maybe 30 seconds

205
00:12:04.920 --> 00:12:06.000
and that was long for myself

206
00:12:06.080 --> 00:12:08.840
and he said certain things
that you can do

207
00:12:08.920 --> 00:12:10.200
and then try again.

208
00:12:11.520 --> 00:12:14.560
[KLOPP]: He explained them
how to cool down your mindset

209
00:12:14.880 --> 00:12:17.040
how to bring yourself
in maybe a happier place

210
00:12:17.400 --> 00:12:18.720
that you can do that longer.

211
00:12:20.320 --> 00:12:22.680
I remember the change
was already massive

212
00:12:22.760 --> 00:12:25.600
and there were some players
that were down for two

213
00:12:25.680 --> 00:12:27.160
or two and a half minutes
on the water

214
00:12:27.240 --> 00:12:30.040
almost three minutes,
and I was like, how?

215
00:12:30.320 --> 00:12:31.480
That was absolutely incredible.

216
00:12:32.880 --> 00:12:35.120
We had players. They did it
for three minutes, then.

217
00:12:35.360 --> 00:12:39.040
Three minutes
after half an hour teaching.

218
00:12:40.920 --> 00:12:44.120
That only means that
you can much more perform

219
00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:45.080
than you ever imagined.

220
00:12:52.160 --> 00:12:53.520
[ATKINSON]: It's Neil Atkinson
and John Gibbons

221
00:12:53.600 --> 00:12:55.600
with the Anfield Wrap. Do you
know how many supporters

222
00:12:55.680 --> 00:12:56.840
we've got worldwide?

223
00:12:57.120 --> 00:12:59.480
[GIBBONS]:
Close to 100 million.

224
00:12:59.760 --> 00:13:00.840
[ATKINSON]:
Believe it or not

225
00:13:00.920 --> 00:13:03.920
it is 450 million people
on the globe.

226
00:13:07.640 --> 00:13:09.200
[MAN]: It's about six o'clock
in the morning

227
00:13:09.720 --> 00:13:11.800
and it's going to be a big,
big turnout

228
00:13:11.880 --> 00:13:13.200
and we're all...
all very excited.

229
00:13:14.400 --> 00:13:15.560
[WOMAN]:
So we woke up early

230
00:13:15.880 --> 00:13:17.360
to come to the pub
to watch the game

231
00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:18.560
and then we're going
straight to school.

232
00:13:23.160 --> 00:13:26.000
[IN PORTUGUESE]:

233
00:13:43.480 --> 00:13:45.560
[GIRL]: Watching Liverpool
on the weekends

234
00:13:45.920 --> 00:13:46.800
it's a family time.

235
00:13:48.400 --> 00:13:51.200
[BOY]: I usually watch
either Salah or Mane

236
00:13:51.280 --> 00:13:52.880
because we are both strikers.

237
00:13:53.640 --> 00:13:56.680
I watch and learn
and then I put it in games.

238
00:13:58.680 --> 00:13:59.760
[MAN]: Going to the match
with your son

239
00:13:59.840 --> 00:14:01.200
is just the most special thing.

240
00:14:02.760 --> 00:14:04.360
We normally get in
half an hour before

241
00:14:04.480 --> 00:14:06.480
stand on The Kop,
then you sing the songs.

242
00:14:08.080 --> 00:14:09.560
When the ball hits the net,
it's incredible.

243
00:14:09.840 --> 00:14:10.960
It's an absolutely
special feeling.

244
00:14:13.040 --> 00:14:15.240
There's no place in the world
I'd rather be than at Anfield

245
00:14:15.320 --> 00:14:16.400
with my ten-year-old.

246
00:14:26.120 --> 00:14:34.000
[CROWD CHANTS]:
♪ You'll never walk alone ♪

247
00:14:34.120 --> 00:14:40.280
♪ Walk on, walk on with hope
in your hearts ♪

248
00:14:41.040 --> 00:14:45.920
♪ And you'll never walk alone ♪

249
00:14:46.600 --> 00:14:52.120
♪ You'll never walk alone ♪

250
00:14:56.200 --> 00:14:58.320
[KLOPP]: It's a while ago
that we played at Anfield.

251
00:14:59.400 --> 00:15:01.600
You have to make Anfield
a fortress again.

252
00:15:02.280 --> 00:15:04.440
Using your own crowd,
using the atmosphere.

253
00:15:07.240 --> 00:15:11.440
[SHOUTING AND CLAPPING]
- [MAN]: Come on, boys, come on!

254
00:15:13.160 --> 00:15:15.360
[CROWD CHEERS]
- [COMMENTATOR]: Here they come.

255
00:15:15.440 --> 00:15:16.840
It all starts here.

256
00:15:17.920 --> 00:15:19.360
[VAN DIJK]: You need
to get into a rhythm.

257
00:15:19.480 --> 00:15:21.000
You need to get into a groove.

258
00:15:23.520 --> 00:15:25.920
You see me
always looking at the Kop

259
00:15:26.000 --> 00:15:27.120
when they play the song

260
00:15:28.200 --> 00:15:30.720
because I just want
to soak it in, enjoy it.

261
00:15:31.120 --> 00:15:38.280
[CHANTING CONTINUES]:
♪ You'll never walk alone ♪

262
00:15:41.520 --> 00:15:42.800
[WHISTLE BLOWS]

263
00:15:44.440 --> 00:15:45.880
[COMMENTATOR]:
The Premier League season

264
00:15:46.400 --> 00:15:47.960
is underway for Liverpool.

265
00:15:49.240 --> 00:15:51.680
There's a long road ahead.

266
00:15:52.920 --> 00:15:55.280
Who knows what waits
at the end of that road.

267
00:15:56.080 --> 00:15:57.960
You can never guess
with this football club

268
00:15:58.040 --> 00:15:59.040
that's for sure.

269
00:16:01.640 --> 00:16:02.640
Robertson.

270
00:16:05.120 --> 00:16:06.840
Origi, it's a lovely ball
by Roberston

271
00:16:06.920 --> 00:16:08.200
really got some weight on it

272
00:16:08.720 --> 00:16:10.520
gives Origi
something to work with.

273
00:16:11.480 --> 00:16:14.120
And he does! The first goal of
Liverpool's new season!

274
00:16:14.240 --> 00:16:18.640
[CROWD CHEERS]
- It's an own goal.

275
00:16:24.920 --> 00:16:28.640
[CROWD CHANTS]: Divock Origi!
- Salah gets it.

276
00:16:29.360 --> 00:16:32.360
Deflection takes it to Firmino,
Salah's in!

277
00:16:32.680 --> 00:16:36.040
Goal for Liverpool!
Goal for Mohamed Salah.

278
00:16:41.880 --> 00:16:44.480
[ALISSON IN PORTUGUESE]:

279
00:16:59.480 --> 00:17:00.560
[COMMENTATOR]
Buendia.

280
00:17:00.880 --> 00:17:01.960
Stiepermann.

281
00:17:03.480 --> 00:17:05.200
Carried away by Alisson.

282
00:17:05.440 --> 00:17:06.880
No problem for 'em.

283
00:17:14.720 --> 00:17:17.240
He's scored one.
Now, can Salah assist one?

284
00:17:19.840 --> 00:17:22.520
Oh, there it is!
Virgil van Dijk, opening night!

285
00:17:22.760 --> 00:17:24.200
How about that! Bang!

286
00:17:31.000 --> 00:17:33.760
It's now Liverpool three,
Norwich City nil.

287
00:17:42.240 --> 00:17:43.520
[COMMENTATOR]:
He's put the ball at his feet.

288
00:17:43.840 --> 00:17:44.840
Goal kick.

289
00:17:49.360 --> 00:17:51.320
Now there is a concern
for Liverpool.

290
00:18:00.760 --> 00:18:02.360
Golden glove winner last season

291
00:18:02.440 --> 00:18:03.960
played every minute
of the Premier League.

292
00:18:04.440 --> 00:18:07.160
It doesn't bode well
for Alisson Becker this.

293
00:18:08.600 --> 00:18:09.560
Don't know what it is.

294
00:18:10.680 --> 00:18:12.160
It's a slip, isn't it?

295
00:18:12.240 --> 00:18:15.160
Straight away put his hands
to his knee.

296
00:18:16.520 --> 00:18:19.360
[SPEAKS PORTUGUESE]:

297
00:18:33.520 --> 00:18:35.480
[KLOPP]: If you ask me
what could have been worse.

298
00:18:36.560 --> 00:18:37.720
Nothing, pretty much.

299
00:18:43.360 --> 00:18:45.400
The situation
was especially difficult

300
00:18:45.480 --> 00:18:48.360
because I think
two weeks before...

301
00:18:50.920 --> 00:18:52.560
[TAPE REWINDS]

302
00:18:54.680 --> 00:18:57.040
Simon Mignolet
came in my office

303
00:18:57.320 --> 00:19:00.640
and told me, "Boss,
I have a big opportunity.

304
00:19:00.720 --> 00:19:01.840
I can go back to Belgium.

305
00:19:01.920 --> 00:19:04.560
I can play for Club Brugge
and I really want to do that".

306
00:19:05.320 --> 00:19:09.040
You know, that's pretty late,
we start next week!

307
00:19:09.520 --> 00:19:12.360
"Yeah, I know,
but it's I want to go back.

308
00:19:12.520 --> 00:19:13.400
Spoke to my wife".

309
00:19:14.080 --> 00:19:15.880
OK. No problem.
Ali is fit.

310
00:19:17.000 --> 00:19:19.200
Number three goalkeeper
in that moment.

311
00:19:19.960 --> 00:19:24.480
Caoimhin Kelleher had a bicycle
accident on holiday.

312
00:19:24.560 --> 00:19:26.000
[LORRY HOOTS]
- [METAL CRASHES]

313
00:19:28.280 --> 00:19:29.280
Broke his...

314
00:19:30.280 --> 00:19:33.040
I think his hand, which is
really bad for a goalie.

315
00:19:34.680 --> 00:19:36.400
So you go through the market,
bam-bam-bam

316
00:19:36.480 --> 00:19:38.440
you look,
which goalkeeper's free

317
00:19:39.480 --> 00:19:41.640
and is good especially
but good and free.

318
00:19:42.120 --> 00:19:43.480
[COMMENTATOR]:
To give him his full title

319
00:19:43.560 --> 00:19:45.800
Adrian San Miguel del Castillo

320
00:19:46.520 --> 00:19:49.160
thirty-two years old
from Seville.

321
00:19:49.600 --> 00:19:52.320
He never expected a club
the stature of Liverpool

322
00:19:52.400 --> 00:19:53.400
to come for him.

323
00:19:54.480 --> 00:19:58.360
[KLOPP]: Adrian trained for
four days, five days with us.

324
00:19:58.560 --> 00:20:00.560
Before that,
he trained by himself.

325
00:20:01.640 --> 00:20:03.440
He didn't play for a year

326
00:20:04.000 --> 00:20:07.520
and then first game,
Alli kicks the ball, and out.

327
00:20:07.880 --> 00:20:09.280
And then wow.

328
00:20:12.040 --> 00:20:14.680
And we had no time to have
these individual talks

329
00:20:14.760 --> 00:20:16.280
and stuff like this
because it was like...

330
00:20:20.120 --> 00:20:21.960
[CROWD CHEERS]

331
00:20:26.840 --> 00:20:28.520
[COMMENTATOR]: Well they're
coming again here Norwich.

332
00:20:29.360 --> 00:20:30.800
Great save by the goalkeeper.

333
00:20:33.160 --> 00:20:34.960
Save from Adrian.

334
00:20:37.200 --> 00:20:41.000
That's the unbelievable
difficult situation.

335
00:20:41.320 --> 00:20:42.800
Like getting from the sofa

336
00:20:42.880 --> 00:20:46.480
and putting your best
performance ever on the pitch

337
00:20:46.560 --> 00:20:47.440
and that's what he did.

338
00:20:47.520 --> 00:20:49.200
[COMMENTATOR] Well, quite
the start for Liverpool.

339
00:20:49.280 --> 00:20:52.160
First three points of
the new season are theirs.

340
00:20:52.240 --> 00:20:53.560
Ward Prowse to deliver.

341
00:20:54.800 --> 00:20:55.840
Comes all the way to--

342
00:20:55.920 --> 00:20:57.880
That's an astonishing save
by Adrian.

343
00:20:59.360 --> 00:21:00.240
Valeri.

344
00:21:01.720 --> 00:21:03.840
That's a really good stop
by Adrian.

345
00:21:04.160 --> 00:21:07.760
Liverpool's great start
to the new season continues.

346
00:21:22.280 --> 00:21:25.000
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

347
00:21:25.120 --> 00:21:28.200
[KLOPP]:

348
00:21:42.080 --> 00:21:43.840
[LIJNDERS]: Seven players
on this side

349
00:21:44.160 --> 00:21:46.160
eight players on the far side.

350
00:21:47.680 --> 00:21:49.760
Both of you ready
to receive behind the cones.

351
00:21:49.840 --> 00:21:51.040
So here Adam ready.

352
00:21:51.600 --> 00:21:53.600
Now be ready because
you can play here or there.

353
00:21:53.880 --> 00:21:54.720
And from there, we start.

354
00:21:58.280 --> 00:21:59.360
[KLOPP] Pretty much everything
in football

355
00:21:59.440 --> 00:22:01.840
is about organisation
and defending.

356
00:22:02.600 --> 00:22:04.240
Because even when
you are attacking

357
00:22:04.320 --> 00:22:07.400
you need players who are
prepared for the moment

358
00:22:07.480 --> 00:22:08.800
when we have to defend again.

359
00:22:12.520 --> 00:22:13.520
[MAN SHOUTS]

360
00:22:15.600 --> 00:22:17.240
Trent, no here, support!

361
00:22:18.200 --> 00:22:20.720
Form some support lines!
Support!

362
00:22:20.960 --> 00:22:23.360
[KLOPP]: So defending is
incredibly important.

363
00:22:24.920 --> 00:22:28.680
You can only feel free in life
if you have kind of protection.

364
00:22:30.400 --> 00:22:32.160
[LJINDERS]:
Not on the same line, Trent!

365
00:22:34.800 --> 00:22:37.280
[KLOPP]: What I want us to be
is feeling completely free

366
00:22:37.360 --> 00:22:39.440
because we know whatever
mistake we make

367
00:22:39.520 --> 00:22:40.960
there is at least one, two

368
00:22:41.040 --> 00:22:45.040
three guys who will sort that
in first instance for us.

369
00:22:45.920 --> 00:22:46.800
Trent!

370
00:22:48.840 --> 00:22:50.200
Support here.
- [INDISTINCT SHOUTING]

371
00:22:51.680 --> 00:22:54.440
[KLOPP]: We want to have
as many players as possible

372
00:22:54.520 --> 00:22:57.520
who can completely focus on
the offensive situation.

373
00:22:59.200 --> 00:23:00.360
[INDISTINCT SHOUTING]

374
00:23:06.520 --> 00:23:08.600
[COMMENTATOR]:
And it's on to Sadio Mane.

375
00:23:08.680 --> 00:23:09.720
[CROWD CHEERS]

376
00:23:09.800 --> 00:23:11.320
Absolutely delightful.

377
00:23:11.680 --> 00:23:14.640
Mane is my favourite player
because he's really fast.

378
00:23:14.720 --> 00:23:16.400
He's a really great winger.

379
00:23:18.400 --> 00:23:21.480
[COMMENTATOR]:
On towards Mane! Oh yes!

380
00:23:21.560 --> 00:23:24.840
[CROWD CHEERS]

381
00:23:26.600 --> 00:23:28.680
[SADIO MANE IN FRENCH]:

382
00:23:43.360 --> 00:23:44.360
[COMMENTATOR]:
Salah.

383
00:23:46.400 --> 00:23:50.280
Firmino, ah, brilliant.
Salah... Salah!

384
00:23:53.040 --> 00:23:55.800
[CROWD CHANTS]:
♪ Mo Salah! Mo Salah! ♪

385
00:23:55.880 --> 00:24:01.360
♪ Running down the wing.
The Egyptian King ♪

386
00:24:01.880 --> 00:24:04.560
[AHMED CAIRO IN ARABIC]:

387
00:24:06.160 --> 00:24:07.400
[CROWD CHEERS]

388
00:24:27.120 --> 00:24:28.880
[COMMENTATOR]:
Mo Salah, coming into the area.

389
00:24:28.960 --> 00:24:30.400
Mo Salah coming through!

390
00:24:30.640 --> 00:24:32.760
[CROWD CHEERS]

391
00:24:32.920 --> 00:24:35.920
[KLOPP]: I love the fact that
we are so much multi-culti.

392
00:24:41.800 --> 00:24:44.320
Having I would say
the best ambassadors

393
00:24:44.800 --> 00:24:47.280
for being a Muslim in the team
is really great.

394
00:24:49.800 --> 00:24:51.640
I think I need better opponent.

395
00:24:52.560 --> 00:24:53.760
Robbo always lose.

396
00:24:55.320 --> 00:24:57.880
[SADIO MANE SPEAKS FRENCH]:

397
00:25:11.720 --> 00:25:14.640
[KLOPP]: Muslims wash
their body very often

398
00:25:14.720 --> 00:25:16.400
in specific situations.

399
00:25:16.960 --> 00:25:18.680
Before warming up,
after warming up

400
00:25:18.760 --> 00:25:20.320
stuff like this,
it takes time.

401
00:25:21.120 --> 00:25:24.280
And so we decided
to do things differently.

402
00:25:25.600 --> 00:25:27.560
It's really not a problem,
we only adjusted our--

403
00:25:27.640 --> 00:25:28.880
when do we arrive in a stadium

404
00:25:28.960 --> 00:25:30.480
and when do we go back
in the dressing room

405
00:25:30.560 --> 00:25:34.240
after warming up
to these rituals?

406
00:25:35.400 --> 00:25:38.240
It costs us
exactly two minutes.

407
00:25:38.720 --> 00:25:41.080
And it's easy to give
these two minutes away

408
00:25:41.160 --> 00:25:43.560
that they can do what is
in this moment for them

409
00:25:43.760 --> 00:25:45.320
absolutely important.

410
00:25:47.760 --> 00:25:49.680
[REPORTER]: Brendan Rodgers'
first return to Anfield

411
00:25:49.760 --> 00:25:52.400
almost four years
to the day since his departure

412
00:25:52.480 --> 00:25:55.320
has made Leicester City
contenders once again.

413
00:25:55.640 --> 00:25:57.920
And with that in mind,
Leicester will be a real threat

414
00:25:58.000 --> 00:26:00.320
to Liverpool's perfect start
to the season today.

415
00:26:01.520 --> 00:26:02.680
[PRESS]:
It's obviously four years

416
00:26:02.760 --> 00:26:04.480
since Brendan Rodgers
left Liverpool.

417
00:26:05.240 --> 00:26:06.800
So what kind of welcome
can he expect

418
00:26:06.880 --> 00:26:08.520
on his first return to Anfield?

419
00:26:09.400 --> 00:26:11.880
[KLOPP]: The reception,
I think, will be good from us.

420
00:26:12.800 --> 00:26:15.760
But still,
is that not a friendly game?

421
00:26:15.840 --> 00:26:20.120
[CROWD ROARS]

422
00:26:26.040 --> 00:26:27.240
[WHISTLE BLOWS]

423
00:26:30.080 --> 00:26:31.480
[COMMENTATOR]:
Potential from Mane.

424
00:26:31.560 --> 00:26:32.960
Really, really good.

425
00:26:35.160 --> 00:26:38.200
[KLOPP]: The most obvious thing,
what people see

426
00:26:38.280 --> 00:26:41.080
that I am very animated,
constantly grinding my teeth

427
00:26:41.160 --> 00:26:42.440
and stuff like this.

428
00:26:43.440 --> 00:26:46.160
I cannot look overnight
like a thinker.

429
00:26:46.440 --> 00:26:48.320
Standing the 90 minutes
out there

430
00:26:49.000 --> 00:26:51.160
and watching a game like this
and everybody thinks

431
00:26:51.520 --> 00:26:54.960
"Oh, obviously something
must be going on his mind".

432
00:26:56.680 --> 00:26:57.640
Then specific moments

433
00:26:57.720 --> 00:26:59.760
I still look like a complete
idiot on the side-line.

434
00:26:59.840 --> 00:27:00.840
I know that.

435
00:27:01.360 --> 00:27:03.160
I had my moments.

436
00:27:03.680 --> 00:27:06.440
That's why I'm probably still
a record holder in Germany

437
00:27:06.520 --> 00:27:08.720
for red cards for managers

438
00:27:08.800 --> 00:27:12.120
and for sure I paid them
the highest fines

439
00:27:12.200 --> 00:27:13.840
in the history
of German Bundesliga.

440
00:27:15.520 --> 00:27:18.280
Irony doesn't help as well,
on the side-line, obviously.

441
00:27:18.520 --> 00:27:21.240
So the referees cannot really
deal with that.

442
00:27:21.520 --> 00:27:23.160
[HE LAUGHS]

443
00:27:23.800 --> 00:27:25.160
I said once

444
00:27:25.240 --> 00:27:26.920
I think my first red card
as a coach I got

445
00:27:27.000 --> 00:27:28.240
I went to the linesman

446
00:27:28.320 --> 00:27:31.600
and ask him how many
wrong decisions are allowed.

447
00:27:31.880 --> 00:27:35.240
Because if it's 15,
we have one left.

448
00:27:35.640 --> 00:27:37.560
And he raised his flag

449
00:27:37.640 --> 00:27:40.240
and I was already
on the way to the stands.

450
00:27:41.320 --> 00:27:43.480
But I calmed down.

451
00:27:45.720 --> 00:27:46.800
[COMMENTATOR]:
Working harder.

452
00:27:46.880 --> 00:27:48.360
Oh, that's broken through.

453
00:27:48.440 --> 00:27:50.920
It's broken through
for Sadio Mane!

454
00:27:51.000 --> 00:27:53.440
[CROWD CHEERS]

455
00:27:53.520 --> 00:27:55.640
Just unstoppable.

456
00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:03.600
Albrighton has nicely picked out
Ayoze Perez.

457
00:28:03.680 --> 00:28:05.440
And here's the chance
for Maddison!

458
00:28:06.440 --> 00:28:10.280
And it's James Maddison who
gets it through the goalkeeper

459
00:28:10.560 --> 00:28:13.080
to level things up
for Leicester City.

460
00:28:14.640 --> 00:28:18.520
Hamza Choudhury will step on
for James Maddison

461
00:28:18.600 --> 00:28:19.600
the goal scorer.

462
00:28:27.760 --> 00:28:29.120
Salah with Soyuncu.

463
00:28:29.920 --> 00:28:31.320
Salah's done it...

464
00:28:54.880 --> 00:28:56.520
[REPORTER]: Is Mo OK?
What's the latest?

465
00:28:56.880 --> 00:28:58.080
How can he be OK?

466
00:28:58.280 --> 00:29:00.200
He limping off the pitch
you ask me if he's OK?

467
00:29:00.280 --> 00:29:01.400
How can he be OK?

468
00:29:01.520 --> 00:29:03.440
Did you watch it back?
It would be...

469
00:29:03.520 --> 00:29:04.400
What do you think?

470
00:29:05.240 --> 00:29:06.720
[REPORTER]:
Well, he was caught from behind.

471
00:29:06.800 --> 00:29:08.360
But I just wondered
if you got an update

472
00:29:08.440 --> 00:29:10.200
in terms of what the injury is.
What has he got?

473
00:29:11.000 --> 00:29:12.800
We don't know.
How should I know now, huh?

474
00:29:15.840 --> 00:29:17.880
[KLOPP]:
Makes me very angry.

475
00:29:18.400 --> 00:29:20.680
I have no problem
with challenges in football

476
00:29:20.760 --> 00:29:22.280
because it's a contact sport.

477
00:29:22.360 --> 00:29:24.400
But this boy
I was very angry with

478
00:29:24.480 --> 00:29:27.120
because two weeks before,
he injured another player

479
00:29:27.480 --> 00:29:29.800
and he came on
and was overly aggressive.

480
00:29:30.280 --> 00:29:31.720
In these moments,
I'm really angry.

481
00:29:31.800 --> 00:29:33.000
I can't describe it
in a different way

482
00:29:33.080 --> 00:29:35.360
because it's the 100% truth.
I don't like it.

483
00:29:36.400 --> 00:29:38.080
[COMMENTATOR]:
Salah's day is done.

484
00:29:39.400 --> 00:29:41.600
[KLOPP]: I cannot really deal
with unfairness

485
00:29:42.000 --> 00:29:44.200
when I feel it's unfair

486
00:29:44.280 --> 00:29:47.520
for some reason, these are
things I cannot really...

487
00:29:48.800 --> 00:29:51.400
I couldn't at all deal with.

488
00:29:54.600 --> 00:29:55.560
[COMMENTATOR]:
Origi.

489
00:29:56.320 --> 00:29:57.880
Lovely piece of control.

490
00:29:59.960 --> 00:30:02.040
Really good cover.
Oh, where you going?

491
00:30:02.480 --> 00:30:03.920
It's Mane, goes down

492
00:30:04.000 --> 00:30:06.640
penalty kick for Liverpool!
- [CROWD CHEERS]

493
00:30:06.800 --> 00:30:08.320
Here comes the late drama!

494
00:30:08.640 --> 00:30:09.840
[WOMAN]:
He's touched him there!

495
00:30:14.480 --> 00:30:15.560
[COMMENTATOR]:
Penalty kick!

496
00:30:15.640 --> 00:30:16.720
[CROWD CHEERS]

497
00:30:16.800 --> 00:30:18.880
[WHISTLE BLOWS]

